n Navigator category#Related":[809,812],"#Application Navigator category#Related#{1}":[811,812]},"outlinks":[{"title":"application scope","target":"c_ApplicationScope","line":60},{"title":"Create an application menu","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/application-development/automated-test-framework-atf/test-steps-app-navigator-category.md","line":141},{"title":"configure the form","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/configure-form-layout.md","line":175},{"title":"Create modules","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/application-development/automated-test-framework-atf/test-steps-app-navigator-category.md","line":179},{"title":"Encoding module URIs","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/application-development/automated-test-framework-atf/test-steps-app-navigator-category.md","line":257},{"title":"Module link types","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/application-development/automated-test-framework-atf/test-steps-app-navigator-category.md","line":273},{"title":"Encoding module URIs","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/application-development/automated-test-framework-atf/test-steps-app-navigator-category.md","line":297},{"title":"Create a survey module","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/servicenow-platform/t_CreatingASurveyModule.md","line":327},{"title":"Create a content page","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-user-interface/t_CreateAContentPage.md","line":335},{"title":"View management","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-user-interface/view-management-overview.md","line":370},{"title":"Create a module for a template","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/t_CreateAModuleForATemplate.md","line":395},{"title":"Timeline pages","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/c_TimelinePages.md","line":453},{"title":"Create a module","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/application-development/automated-test-framework-atf/test-steps-app-navigator-category.md","line":710},{"title":"Create a module","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/application-development/automated-test-framework-atf/test-steps-app-navigator-category.md","line":807},{"title":"Application scope","target":"c_ApplicationScope","line":811}],"metadata":{"title":"Application Navigator category","description":"Verify the functionality of menus and modules in the application navigator.Verifies the visibility, or lack thereof, of selected application menus in the application navigator \\(left navigation bar\\). For example, you create a test that first impersonates a user, then verifies that specified application menus \\(such as Self-Service and Reports\\) are visible, or are not visible, to that user.Application menus define the main content that users can access in the application navigator. You can configure which applications appear in the application navigator.Modules are the children, or the second tier navigation options to the applications in the application navigator. Modules often link to other pages or records in the platform. You can configure which modules appear in the application navigator using Application Menus module.The Link type field on the Module form specifies what type of link the module opens.Clicking a module name in the navigation pane executes a URI that opens the module's page in the content pane. All the characters in module URIs must be URL-encoded or the link breaks.Verify the visibility, or lack thereof, of selected modules in the application navigator \\(left navigation bar\\). For example, create a test that first impersonates a user, then verifies that specified modules \\(such as Homepage and My Requests\\) are visible, or are not visible, to that user.Open a module from the application navigator, as if a user had clicked it. The module must be visible to the currently executing user to navigate to it.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/application-development/automated-test-framework-atf/test-steps-app-navigator-category.html","release":"australia","product":"Automated Test Framework \\(ATF\\)","classification":"automated-test-framework-atf","topic_type":"reference","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":15,"breadcrumb":["Automated Test Framework \\(ATF\\) test step categories","Automated Test Framework \\(ATF\\)","Testing and debugging applications","Building applications"],"tags":["#application-development","#atf","#testing","#automated-tests","#test-suites","#type-reference"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/application-development/automated-test-framework-atf/test-steps-app-navigator-category.md"},
